<title>ZIMBABWE: ZIMBABWE'S TA YR SHR UP, DIV SLIPS.</title>
<headline>ZIMBABWE'S TA YR SHR UP, DIV SLIPS.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended May 31.</p>
<p>	    (million Zimbabwe dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)			  41.0 vs 24.8</p>
<p>    Div (cts)	   5.0 making  8.0 vs 10.0</p>
<p>   Pre-finance charges profit  117.0 vs 149.6</p>
<p>    Finance charges		  59.5 vs 62.4</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		  139.8 vs 101.3</p>
<p>    Taxation			   45.5 vs 42.8</p>
<p>    After-tax profit		 94.2 vs 58.5</p>
<p>    Turnover		  2.7 billion vs 2.2 billion</p>
<p>Div payable October 11</p>
<p>on register September 6.</p>
<p>Full name: TA Holdings Limited </p>
<p>NOTE:- The company said it expected financial charges to</p>
<p>decline in the new year. It added that in line with predictions</p>
<p>by independent economists, the rate of annual inflation --</p>
<p>pegged at 22 percent in July -- and the cost of money were</p>
<p>expected to come down &quot;moderately&quot;.</p>
<p>----Emelia Sithole, Harare Newsroom: +263-4 72 52 27/8/9---</p>
</text>
